{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516079-w5-spanish-crowdfunding-has-been-a-totally-failure","id":1516079,"title":"W5 spanish crowdfunding has been a totally failure.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-25T02:37:24-07:00","id":1516079,"title":"W5 spanish crowdfunding has been a totally failure.","content":"Hi there!<br /> <br /> Tomorrow will finish the spanish crowdfunding of Werewolf 5th edition and it gives a very interesting data about the W5 situation here. I know that every country is a case-by-case scenario (and a very different one from the US market) but with Paradox haven't released any information about the profit of WoD 5th edition yet, maybe this is the most similar thing that we could aspire and compare to the other 20th anniversary books. But like always take all this with a grain of salt. If you have questions about how is the spanish and latin american RPG communities (both are very close to one another), I will be glad to answer your questions. The data is the following:<br /> <br /> W5 (2023): 33,125.30 \u20ac<br /> W20 (2015): 127,000 \u20ac (The information here I obtained from old phorum pages, the wayback machine didn't work for me and the data was erased from official pages. Idk if in the case I post any of my sources I could break any rule of the forum)<br /> <br /> There aren't any info about the sales dates of V5 and H5 because the absence of a crowdfunding. Accord with the editorial the sales of V5 were very good but I think that H5 didn't settle well here and for that reason they decide to went with a crowdfunding this time.<br /> <br /> Data from other 20th anniversary games:<br /> <br /> Wr20 (2020): 78,578.31\u20ac<br /> C20 (2018): 93,486.28\u20ac<br /> M20 (2017): 168,007.96\u20ac<br /> V20 (2014): 178,123.00 \u20ac<br /> <br /> Also I have to add that the situation of the spanish WoD community is a special one here. The thing is that 20th anniversary editions are still in printing and selling in book stores even with the 5th edition arrival in 2018, meanwhile, in the US market the 20th anniversary books are only available through Drivethrurpg. Also CoD 2nd edition doesn't exist here. But I though that this data was interesting enough to share.<br /> <br /> Edit: ortography revition<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","user":"Metalbird","date":". 06-25-2023, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","name":"Metalbird","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T03:48:20-07:00","id":1516086,"title":"","content":"Interesting, could be word of mouth about what we're seeing from development.<br /> <br /> How did v5 go down in Spain after the initial sales I know the v5 backlash took time to gain momentum after bad supplementary releases and the practical limitations of the mechanics became more apparantl over time in the UK. Over here curiosity and cautious optermiism gradually shifted to disappointment and later frustration in my local gaming circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-25-2023, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T05:27:14-07:00","id":1516094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516079-w5-spanish-crowdfunding-has-been-a-totally-failure?p=1516086#post1516086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, could be word of mouth about what we're seeing from development.<br /> <br /> How did v5 go down in Spain after the initial sales I know the v5 backlash took time to gain momentum after bad supplementary releases and the practical limitations of the mechanics became more apparantl over time in the UK. Over hear curiosity and cautious optermiism gradually shifted to disappointment and later frustration in my local gaming circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am from Spain and from what i can tell from my personal experience is that people just act as if V5 and any 5th edition product did not exist. Furthermore they do not want to even discuss it despite knowing the franchise and having played at least V20, which is the popular option and where most of the player base is.<br /> <br /> Note that some people bought it because the hype and the Masquerade being a big name in the franchise but most of them prefer V20 and the negative feedback of V5 has made people distrust white wolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are multiple factor in this but general these are the reasons:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>1) - Cost/Benefit: </b>You can get a translated physical edition + pdf of masquerade at the cost of 20 euros at any comic store (at least that is what I payed at the time, prices might have gone a little up) This is the main reason.<br /> <br /> <b>2) - Lack of Content:</b> V20 has all the clans meanwhile V5 is like a Paradox Game, in the sense it has the minimal content and to get the true experience you have to pay multiple DLCs.<br /> <br /> <b>3) - People dislike the artysle:</b> Vampire has 90s Comic book art that is highly distintive. V5 photographic art is seen as confusing and pretentious. People want to play vampires not Fashion Week Rejecteds.<br /> <br /> <b>4) - People dislike the mechanics:</b> They are seen as restrictive (and they are)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>5) - TTRPG are an oral tradition:</b> In Spain you mostly get into rol because that is what the Game Master plays, most of them play V20, DnD or the Return of the Dragon (Spanish version of DnD which by the way is superior to the original by miles), Chuluth and Aquelarre are also big here.<br /> <br /> <b>6) People think of 5th Edition as requiem 1st Edition:</b> which was a failure so big that you can buy the hardcover edition at a cost of 9,99 EUROS as stores have trouble getting rid of it. Note that personally I think blood and smoke or Requiem 2nd Edition have the best mechanics of the genre.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>7) Roleplaying is A niche Hobby:</b> You cannot triumph by having the community against you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Add to all those factors that in Spain the economy barely works for the middle to low classes, while the country is the best place in the world to live, there is very little work and a lot of unenployees. This causes work conditions to become worse because there are many applicants. Add to that abusive taxes to keep a giant state and buro-&quot;crazy&quot;, perpetuated by cinic politicians that do not care about the people in both sides of the political spectrum, as showcased by bad use of public funds and sometimes outright corruption.<br /> <br /> So people become very careful to choose in what they invest their money and time, as consecuence getting new costumers in such niche market is thus a near imposible task, specially if you dismised your old customers and your product is seen as expensive for what it offers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 06-25-2023, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T11:06:06-07:00","id":1516112,"title":"","content":"I mean, it funded and hit a stretch goal so it can\u2019t be a total failure. Plus it\u2019s got 100 more backers and raised like 10k Euros more than the French one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T11:48:56-07:00","id":1516115,"title":"","content":"Its not a failure based on the tiny amount they were trying to raise, but its definitely very small numbers compared to most TTRPG 'Kickstarters' linked to a known IP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T12:24:46-07:00","id":1516117,"title":"","content":"Yeah... maybe called it failure was too harsh for my part, sorry for that :S. But as the same time, I don't think that Paradox is going after this small quantities and is concerning that Wraith ,which is always considered like a very minor game line compared to the big three, got better in its crowdfunding than this new edition. Also W5 hasn't collected even the half of the money than W20 did. But well maybe its too early to made any statement for my part because the crowdfunding isn't over, maybe we could have a surprise tomorrow. Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","name":"Metalbird","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T08:54:16-07:00","id":1516215,"title":"","content":"There are, still 6 hours to go, and it has reached 37.000, it may still go up a bit but it will probably stop just under 40 000.<br /> <br /> As a Wod5 supporter and someone who has worked in two RPG Kickstarters in Italy, I wouldn't call the French and Spanish W5 Kickstarters &quot;total failures&quot;, but they probably are not up to the franchise potential, especially the French one.<br /> <br /> A 25 000 - 40 000 range in a single European market is a solid result, higher than indie productions (which range into the 10 000 - 20 000 euros), but lower than &quot; RPG of the year&quot; products (like Household or Broken Compass) or of a successful 5e product (which can reach and surpass 100 000 euros, even though they are usually multilingual products). <br /> <br /> Retail printings of a corebook are usually around 1000 copies, and both publishers are well known and with a dedicated Wod fanbase, so probably W5 should have performed better. <br /> <br /> Still, a 30-40% preorder it's good enough for a localized product (so only translation and printing costs), but W5 probably will not be the hype of the year in those two countries. <br /> <br /> I wonder how it will fare in Italy, considering W20 was the only edition ever of WtA to arrive on the market, with just the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T23:45:40-07:00","id":1516323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516079-w5-spanish-crowdfunding-has-been-a-totally-failure?p=1516215#post1516215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are, still 6 hours to go, and it has reached 37.000, it may still go up a bit but it will probably stop just under 40 000.<br /> <br /> As a Wod5 supporter and someone who has worked in two RPG Kickstarters in Italy, I wouldn't call the French and Spanish W5 Kickstarters &quot;total failures&quot;, but they probably are not up to the franchise potential, especially the French one.<br /> <br /> A 25 000 - 40 000 range in a single European market is a solid result, higher than indie productions (which range into the 10 000 - 20 000 euros), but lower than &quot; RPG of the year&quot; products (like Household or Broken Compass) or of a successful 5e product (which can reach and surpass 100 000 euros, even though they are usually multilingual products).<br /> <br /> Retail printings of a corebook are usually around 1000 copies, and both publishers are well known and with a dedicated Wod fanbase, so probably W5 should have performed better.<br /> <br /> Still, a 30-40% preorder it's good enough for a localized product (so only translation and printing costs), but W5 probably will not be the hype of the year in those two countries.<br /> <br /> I wonder how it will fare in Italy, considering W20 was the only edition ever of WtA to arrive on the market, with just the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 was extremely well perceived in Italy , on the other hand w20 was a failure, but only because the local company that translated it did a very bad job, both for translation and customer service.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 06-27-2023, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}